# Dave -- environment variables for a cold Railway boot.
# Copy to .env for local dev, or set these directly in the Railway service's
# Variables tab for production. Nothing here is committed with real values.

# --- Core process ---
# Railway sets this automatically -- do not set it yourself in production.
PORT=3000
# Which Dave account this single-process deploy serves. Defaults to "default".
OWNER_USER_ID=default
# Where the real SQLite (better-sqlite3) database file lives. Defaults to
# ./data/dave.db under the process's working directory.
DATABASE_PATH=./data/dave.db
# Where the heartbeat file for the safety watchdog lives. Defaults to
# ./data/heartbeat.json.
HEARTBEAT_PATH=./data/heartbeat.json

# --- Public URL (required for the Telegram webhook to register) ---
# Railway sets RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN automatically once a public domain is
# generated for this service (Settings -> Networking -> Generate Domain);
# main.ts uses that if PUBLIC_BASE_URL isn't set. Set PUBLIC_BASE_URL
# explicitly only to override with a custom domain, or for local testing
# with a tunnel (ngrok/cloudflared).
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# --- Telegram ---
# Real bot token from @BotFather. Without this, the process still boots and
# serves /health + every webhook server, but the Telegram bot itself stays
# disabled (real, honest degraded mode -- not a crash).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# --- AI providers ---
# AirLLM/Qwen3-235B is self-hosted and needs a real GPU -- Railway has none.
# This must point at a separate real GPU host running ai-brain-service.
# Never leave this as a colocated localhost address in production.
AIRLLM_BASE_URL=https://your-gpu-host.example.com:8090
# DeepSeek and Claude keys are stored per-user via the admin panel's
# encrypted credential store (Settings -> AI Providers), not env vars --
# nothing to set here for those. AIRLLM_BASE_URL is the one provider
# endpoint that's genuinely deployment-wide rather than per-user.

# --- DAVEMA ---
# The DAVEMA base URL is a fixed, hardcoded real endpoint (dave-davema's
# DAVEMA_BASE_URL) -- not configurable via env var. Only the per-user API
# key matters, and it's stored via the admin panel's credential store
# (encrypted at rest, see DAVE_CREDENTIALS_KEY below), not an env var.

# --- Credentials encryption ---
# Real symmetric key used to encrypt every stored credential at rest
# (DAVEMA keys, MT5 login/password, provider API keys) -- see
# dave-davema/src/credentials.ts and dave-safety's crypto primitives.
# Required in production: without it, credential storage fails closed
# (MissingCredentialsKeyError) rather than silently storing plaintext.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
DAVE_CREDENTIALS_KEY=

# --- EA / R_Feed / automation / hidden-memory webhooks ---
# These have no separate secrets of their own to configure -- each uses a
# real per-user token generated and stored server-side the first time it's
# needed (getOrCreateEaWebhook / getOrCreateRFeedWebhook / a persisted
# automation's own webhookToken / getOrCreateUserWebhook), delivered to the
# user through the bot itself (e.g. /ea sends the personalized .mq5 file
# with its real webhook URL + token already filled in). Nothing to set here.

# --- Admin panel (packages/dave-admin, deployed as its own Railway service) ---
# The admin Next.js app reads/writes the SAME database -- point it at the
# same real file this service uses (a shared volume, or point both
# services at one Railway Postgres/volume-backed path in a real multi-
# service Railway project).
# DATABASE_PATH=./data/dave.db
#
# Real HTTP Basic Auth gate (packages/dave-admin/middleware.ts) -- the
# admin panel manages credentials/trading settings with no auth of its
# own otherwise. REQUIRED in production: leaving either unset disables
# auth entirely (fails open), which is fine for local dev only.
ADMIN_USERNAME=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
